{"_v":1,"id":"the-producers-2001","bd":{"positive":2,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2001/04/20/movies/theater-review-frolic-and-detour-on-the-way-to-satire.html","d":"2001-04-20","q":"This most exuberantly entertaining musical comedy to hit Broadway in years has the good sense never to take itself seriously."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/Producers.html","d":"2001-04-20","q":"The Producers is a show that works on every level - as a musical, as a comedy, as a theatrical experience, and as a celebration of what Broadway can be when it really tries."},{"cn":"Steven Winn","o":"San Francisco Chronicle","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/1234293871/","d":"2001-04-20","q":"For all its exuberant, chaotic impulses, then, it's disappointing to report that \"The Producers\" falls considerably short of the bell-ringing delight that advance word had led audiences to expect."}],"au":{"score":91,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"ss":{"s":92,"c":301},"mz":{"s":88,"c":129,"sr":4.4}}},"hi":"/images/shows/the-producers-2001/hero.jpg","ta":"246 W 44th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2001-03-21","ca":[{"n":"Matthew Broderick","r":"Leo Bloom"},{"n":"Nathan Lane","r":"Max Bialystock"},{"n":"Roger Bart","r":"Carmen Ghia"},{"n":"Gary Beach","r":"Roger De Bris"},{"n":"Cady Huffman","r":"Ulla"},{"n":"Brad Oscar","r":"Franz Liebkind"},{"n":"Jeffry Denman","r":"Scott"},{"n":"Madeleine Doherty","r":"Hold-me Touch-me"},{"n":"Bryn Dowling","r":"Usherette"},{"n":"Kathy Fitzgerald","r":"Shirley"},{"n":"Robert H. Fowler","r":"O'Houlihan"},{"n":"Ida Gilliams","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Eric Gunhus","r":"Lead Tenor"},{"n":"Kimberly Hester","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Naomi Kakuk","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Matt Loehr","r":"O'Riley"},{"n":"Peter Marinos","r":"Bryan"},{"n":"Angie L. Schworer","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"J